From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:50:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ship the licences of the ExternalProject-built and in-tree
 vendored dependencies

setup.cfg's `license_files = LICENSE` is an explicit setuptools list, so it
does not fall back to the `LICEN[CS]E*` auto-discovery glob. setup.py builds
with `-DOCIO_INSTALL_EXT_PACKAGES=ALL`, which statically links Imath,
OpenEXR (itself vendoring libdeflate and OpenJPH), expat, pystring,
yaml-cpp, minizip-ng, lcms2, pybind11 and zlib into libOpenColorIO and the
bundled command-line apps; the in-tree src/apputils/argparse.cpp and
strutil.cpp (from OpenImageIO) and ext/sampleicc, ext/xxHash are compiled
in unconditionally. None of their licence texts reach dist-info/licenses
today (confirmed against the published opencolorio 2.5.1 PyPI wheel, which
ships only LICENSE).

Add each dependency's licence text as LICENSE.<dep> at the project root
and widen license_files to also match LICENSE.*, so they land in the
wheel's dist-info/licenses/ with no other packaging change.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; the same gap exists in every opencolorio wheel on PyPI, so this needs a maintainer discussion rather than a drive-by PR]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
